check 1
# A walk in the Rogue Encampment re-targeted by a second click while the
# player still walks (seams/movement-prediction.md §2.1, §2.9;
# sim/pathing.md §1.5): ScnAma, -seed 1234; frame 10 a left click at
# (600, 300) (east), frame 18 a left click at (250, 420) (south-west)
# while the first walk runs, frame 30 a left click at (650, 180)
# (north-east, a reversal) while the second runs. Compare the player's mode, path target and
# position frame by frame. Spec: specs/tools/scenario-diff.md §2 rule 4.
name walk-click-walk-town-ama
save ScnAma --class ama --expansion
seed 1234
ticks 70
seconds 240
channels state packets
input frame 10; click 600 300; frame 18; click 250 420; frame 30; click 650 180
# Every field compared (rc-walk-town: 70/70 equal on integ-r16 without the
# old `ignore seed s fc sp`); packets compared too, so the C->S of the
# clicks is checked against the d2rs client gap (scenario-diff.md open
# question 6).
